# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4 ("Binding groups and cycles": the order of a group's lines decides positions and nothing else), ch. 8 (`<-` binds the clause's plain result; a widget application is transparent) and ruling TC (places counted as built): loud gives 10, so the first clause builds its label at 1 and gives 1, the next label is 2 and the arm's 3; soft gives 20, so the second clause builds nothing and gives 2, and the arm builds nothing.
test loud

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="add")
    1: Ui.Label(text="ten")
    2: Ui.Label(text="wide 1")
    3: Ui.Label(text="x 0")

test soft

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="add")
    1: Ui.Label(text="wide 2")
